Disgrace news
=============

0.1.9
-----
- DSSI plugins now run at the project sample rate. The rate was handed to
  the sandbox once at startup and never updated, because the instrument
  never overrode set_sample_rate(), so a 48 kHz project could drive a
  plugin at 44.1 kHz with wrong pitch and wrong filter/oscillator rates.
  A rate change now re-instantiates the plugin, keeping its control values
  and bank/program selection.
- Fix DSSI plugin audio distorting during playback but sounding correct in
  the instrument view. The sandbox renders one block behind and the reply
  was copied with min(previous_size, nframes), which truncated it when the
  block was shorter and left a gap when it was longer. A JACK callback
  always asks for exactly one period, so the instrument view matched, but
  the sequencer splits periods at tick boundaries, so tracker playback
  dropped and gap-filled samples on every block. The two are now decoupled
  by an output FIFO fed with whole backend periods.
- DSSI sandbox: give every audio port its own buffer (a multi-output
  plugin could read its own output), choose the stereo pair by port name
  (karplong has its outputs at 0 and 5), connect outputs before activate(),
  and reject a plugin without audio outputs instead of loading it silently.
- JACK auto-connect now stays on a single physical device, so a mix cannot
  be spread across two sound cards when the graph carries several; the OSS
  backend honours $AUDIODEV instead of hardcoding /dev/dsp.
- The keyboard spans two-and-a-bit octaves, tracker style: the lower row
  continues ", L . ; /" into the next octave and the upper row continues
  "9 O 0 P" (plus U-umlaut on German layouts), so octave 4 covers C-4..F-6
  instead of C-4..B-5. Notes above B-8 were unreachable and octave 9 was a
  dead setting; the trackable range is now C-0..B-9 and the tracker,
  transpose, notation view, sample root and every importer/exporter follow
  it. The instrument view also played an octave below the tracker and now
  matches it.
- Fix Tab being stolen as a note key: the Ctrl+letter normalisation
  rewrote every key code 1-26, and Tab is 9. Fix the key-capture dialog
  storing modifier bits the lookup never matched, so an assigned shortcut
  with a modifier did not work.

0.1.8
-----
- Fix playback going silent for the rest of the session after a few
  minutes of editing. The sequencer tick phase could underflow when Play
  was pressed while an audio block was being rendered; no tick fired
  afterwards, so the song kept "playing" without sound and the transport
  clock showed a garbage duration. The phase is now updated atomically
  and saturates instead of wrapping, playback starts reset it, and the
  clock clamps its inputs. Resizing a pattern no longer drains the
  Play/Stop command queue from the GUI thread.
- DSSI: a crashed or hung plugin sandbox is now detected and reported
  instead of silently silencing the track forever. The liveness probe
  reaps the child (kill() succeeded on zombies, so a crash was invisible),
  a reload no longer inherits a stuck request, the sandbox stops blocking
  on a full stdout pipe, and plugin startup is bounded by a 15 s timeout.
  Instrument health (Ok / LoadFailed / Crashed / Stalled) and the failure
  reason are exposed for the UI and logged when a project fails to load
  a plugin.

0.1.7
-----
- Subtrack counts are now global per track: adding or removing note
  columns applies to every pattern, and new patterns keep the same
  subtracks instead of resetting to one.

0.1.6
-----
- Guitar tab exporter: new "Export TAB" button renders a track as
  ASCII guitar/bass tab with a tuning dialog (presets plus free
  per-subtrack open strings). Notes sustain until note-off and
  out-of-range notes find the nearest playable string.
- Tracker pattern list rows use sizer layout and no longer scramble
  under the scrollbar at any font or DPI.

0.1.5
-----
- Fix scrambled pattern lengths in the tracker pattern list (duplicate
  rows went stale after resize; the timer rebuild no longer wipes
  half-typed values).
- Restore dead Ctrl+letter shortcuts (Copy/Cut/Paste/Undo/...) in the
  tracker and add an Edit section to its right-click menu.

0.1.3
-----
- Sampler instruments gain a per-sample root note (plus transpose cents):
  the root trigger plays the sample at its recorded speed/pitch and
  transposition stays musical. XRNS import reads Mapping/BaseNote,
  Transpose and Finetune; the sampler editor has a Root control.
- Octave labels follow MIDI/Yamaha convention (60 = C-4) in tracker,
  tracks view and notation, matching Renoise; LilyPond export fixed
  accordingly and live keyboard entry aligns octave numbering.
- Build: default -O3, --enable-lto / --enable-native-march, new
  `make production` target, denormal FTZ/DAZ in the render path.

0.1.2
-----
- Fix off-by-one orphan instrument: new projects start with the default
  track using the default instrument, and XRNS import drops unreferenced
  shared instruments, so repeated track joins no longer leave the
  instrument list one entry longer than necessary.
- Audio engine: lock-free thread-pool fan-out without per-block
  allocations, non-blocking DSSI sandbox handoff, allocation-free
  SFZ/XRNI voice recycling, TTS synthesis kept off the realtime thread,
  cheaper per-sample DSP (cached ADSR/envelope steps, hoisted filter and
  compressor constants, fused copy/gain passes).
- GUI stays responsive on large songs: mixer meters throttled and gated to
  the visible tab, transport bar avoids redundant relayouts, order-list
  copies removed from per-frame drawing, list rebuilds use Freeze/Thaw.

0.1.1
-----
- Deleting a track (including the tracker Join to Previous/Next) now also
  removes its instrument when no other track uses it.
- Joining hands the source instrument over to the target track when the
  target has none, so joined notes stay audible.

0.1.0
-----
Initial public release.
